---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>Hi, I'm Inaya.</h1>
			<p>
				I'm 19 and I've lived near Paris for all of it. I write C, Go and
				TypeScript, mostly because I want to know what's happening underneath.
			</p>
			<p>
				What pulls me is the bottom of the stack. Runtimes, operating systems,
				the seam where firmware hands over to the OS. I'd rather have a system
				I can walk down layer by layer than a fast one I have to take on faith.
			</p>
			<p>
				Before code there were eleven years of art school and then a fine arts
				degree at Paris 1 that I left in May 2025. The degree went. The art
				didn't.
			</p>
			<p>
				Right now I'm doing a BTS SIO SLAM on an apprenticeship contract.
				There's a much longer version of all this on the
				<a href="/about">about page</a>, and whatever I've pushed publicly
				lives on <a href="https://github.com/ZiedYousfi">GitHub</a>.
			</p>
			<p>
				The <a href="/projects">projects page</a> is empty. I'll get to it.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
